    <string name="info_score_title">Sleep score</string>
    <string name="info_score_body">A summary of the night from 0 to 100, made of five parts: duration, efficiency, deep and REM sleep, interruptions and regularity. Each part shows its points and what was measured. The dial\'s arc is the score: a full circle is 100.</string>
    <string name="info_duration_body">How long you were asleep compared with your sleep goal of %1$s. The full %2$d points at or above your goal, and proportionally fewer below it.</string>
    <string name="info_efficiency_body">The share of your time in bed that you were actually asleep. 0 points at %1$d\u00A0%% or less, rising to the full %2$d points at %3$d\u00A0%% or more. Healthy adults usually manage %4$d\u00A0%% or more.</string>
    <string name="info_deep_rem_body">The share of your sleep spent in deep and REM sleep, the stages that matter most for physical recovery and memory. 0 points at %1$d\u00A0%% or less, rising to the full %2$d points at %3$d\u00A0%% or more. It needs sleep stages from Garmin; without them, these points are shared out across the other parts.</string>
    <string name="info_interruptions_body">Starts at %1$d points. Each wake-up (awake for %2$d minutes or more after falling asleep, not counting the last one before you get up) costs %3$d, and each cluster of noise events (events within %4$d minutes of each other) costs %5$d. Never below 0.</string>
    <string name="info_regularity_body">How well you kept your goals that night, each scored from 0 to 1: in bed by %1$s, asleep for %2$s, at most %3$d snoozes, and a steady bedtime over the last %4$d nights. The average of the four, times %5$d.</string>

